From: Surface Overdrive <noreply@surface-overdrive>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu3: the motion map in 8x8 blocks from 2000 pixels wide

The motion map of the software temporal denoiser worked on 4x4 blocks at every size: at 2560x1920 that is
307,000 blocks, about 10 ms a frame on the Surface Go. From 2000 pixels wide the blocks are 8x8, the same detail
of motion as 4x4 at half the size: motion map 8.4 -> 2.9 ms and block sums 2.1 -> 1.1 ms (the filter 20 -> 12.5
ms a frame in good light). The grain is a little lower too (still flicker 0.87 -> 0.75, 1.62 -> 1.45 in the
dark: noise fools the larger blocks less), no trail seen on the recordings of a moving person.
---
